    "raw_text": "Working to keep prescription costs down: holding pharmacy benefit managers accountable\nOctober 15, 2026\nDrug price spikes, at the hands of PBMs (pharmacy benefit managers) is something I've been very vocal about since being in office. PBM reform — needed to stop \"middlemen price gouging\"— on critical consumer prescriptions and reducing prescription drug costs has been a legislative priority. I’m grateful for the Pennsylvania Office of Attorney General for holding them accountable!\nRead my letter to Attorney General Sunday\nhere\nand see this latest article\nto learn more.\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
